{"id":"46019905-ffdf-4626-a242-42d75f5a81de","object":"chat.completion","created":1785025166,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\":\"def solve(case):\\n    edges = case['edges']\\n    refinement = case['refinement']\\n    # Build node -> group mapping\\n    node_to_group = refinement\\n    # Build group -> nodes membership\\n    group_members = {}\\n    for node, group in node_to_group.items():\\n        group_members.setdefault(group, []).append(node)\\n    # Sort each membership list\\n    for group in group_members:\\n        group_members[group].sort()\\n    # Aggregate edges\\n    edge_weights = {}\\n    for u, v, w in edges:\\n        gu = node_to_group[u]\\n        gv = node_to_group[v]\\n        if gu <= gv:\\n            key = (gu, gv)\\n        else:\\n            key = (gv, gu)\\n        edge_weights[key] = edge_weights.get(key, 0) + w\\n    # Build sorted aggregate edges\\n    aggregate_edges = []\\n    for (g1, g2), total in edge_weights.items():\\n        aggregate_edges.append([g1, g2, total])\\n    aggregate_edges.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1]))\\n    return {'aggregate_edges': aggregate_edges, 'members': group_members}\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement `solve(case)` for task DATA-LEI-02. The case payload has edges and refinement. The refinement maps each node to a community group. We need to produce aggregate_edges (list of [source_group, target_group, weight]) where edges are aggregated by mapping nodes to groups, summing weights, and canonicalizing undirected edges (sorted pair?). Also members: dict with keys from refinement values (group names) and values are list of nodes in that group sorted? The output schema says \"dynamicKeysFrom\": \"case.refinement.values()\", so keys must be exactly the values from refinement (the group strings). The values are arrays of strings (node IDs). Should be sorted? The schema says items type string, no mention of order, but the